# ============================================
# Build context for src/NewVixSmart.Web/Dockerfile
#
# The context is ALWAYS the repository root - never src/NewVixSmart.Web - in
# all three callers: docker-compose.yml, .github/workflows/ci.yml and the manual
# `docker build -f src/NewVixSmart.Web/Dockerfile .`. The Dockerfile copies
# global.json, Directory.Build.props and aspire/Vix.ServiceDefaults from the
# root, so a narrower context simply fails to build.
#
# Nothing listed under "KEEP" below may be removed: global.json pins the SDK,
# Directory.Build.props carries TreatWarningsAsErrors / Nullable / ImplicitUsings
# for the publish, and the aspire/ project reference is a real ProjectReference.
# ============================================

# build output
**/bin
**/obj
**/TestResults
test-out*.txt
tests-result.txt
*.log
*.trx
*.coverage

# VCS / IDE / tooling
.git
.github
.vs
.idea
.playwright-cli
node_modules

# Never ship real credentials
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# appsettings.Development.json holds the development JWT signing key and the
# three seed passwords (Admin@123 etc.). NewVixSmart.Web.csproj already sets
# CopyToPublishDirectory="Never" for it, so it is not needed to build or to
# run - but leaving it in the context put it in a builder layer and in the
# local build cache, which is exactly where a leaked key should not be.
**/appsettings.Development.json
**/appsettings.*.local.json
**/secrets.json
**/*.pfx
**/*.p12

# Database dumps and live data files
**/*.bak
**/*.trn
**/*.mdf
**/*.ndf
**/*.ldf
**/*.db
**/*.sqlite
**/*.sqlite3
backups/
artifacts/
screenshots/

# Not needed to build the web image
docs
plan
tests
e2e
design-system
scripts
accessibility.md
ACCESSIBILITY.md
*.md
# aspire/Vix.AppHost is not published; Vix.ServiceDefaults below IS a
# ProjectReference and must stay in the context.
aspire/Vix.AppHost
